  "notes": "The original-sample architect: he writes and records his own vintage source material and then samples it, so every parameter here describes a live-played recording rather than a piano roll. That is the reason for the loosest-but-one humanize on this bench (`quantizeStrength` 0.7, `velocityVar` 0.25), 8th-grid swing at 0.56, and a bass that is `independent_riff` in the 28–47 register with authored cell shapes — the research says the low end is an upright or electric bass from the source recording, not an 808. Harmony is the other half: m7/m9/altered-dominant colour with sevenths at 0.5 and ninths at 0.3, `dissonanceBudget.tritone` 0.3 for the altered dominants, and non-functional-but-tonal families (ii–v–i, i–iv–VII–III, iv–VII–III–VI) that come from what the tape did rather than from theory. The drums are deliberately quiet — `velocityTiers` is pulled *down*, the inverse of T-Minus — because the research says they are secondary to the sampled bed. ⚠ An authored `chords.dissonanceBudget` was removed: no generator reads it, so it was a knob that looked like a parameter and did nothing.",
